# Beacon HTML styling

Full rules: [docs/ui.md](../../docs/ui.md). This overrides the daisyUI skill’s “use Tailwind utilities in HTML” default.

## Allowed

- daisyUI component classes: `btn`, `btn-primary`, `btn-outline`, `alert`, `navbar`, `dock`, `drawer`, `lg:drawer-open`, `menu`, `input`, `select`, `table`, `card`, `badge`, `fieldset`, `dropdown`, `theme-controller`, …
- Named layout: `page`, `stack`, `cluster`, `page-header`, `table-scroll`, `brand-mark`, `no-print`, `print-only`

## Forbidden

```html
<!-- BAD -->
<div class="flex gap-4 p-4 text-sm md:w-1/2">
<button class="btn" style="max-width:28rem">

<!-- GOOD -->
<div class="cluster">
<button class="btn btn-primary">
```

If daisyUI cannot express it, add a named class in CSS and document it in `docs/ui.md`. Do not invent utilities in the template.

## Brand

Header: Rainbow Haven lockup (`web/static/img/rainbow-haven.svg`), `alt="Rainbow Haven"`. Title/footer: Beacon. Do not use rainbow stripe colours on UI chrome. Dark mode: logo on `.brand-mark` chip, never `filter: invert`.
